# Family A21: backoff jitter policies (internal/backoff). See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./internal/backoff
BENCH=BenchmarkBackoff
REF=constant
AUTO_KEY=backoff
ADR=18
TITLE="Backoff jitter (A21)"

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="lowest peak, fast recovery -> full jitter"
# MATRIX=default is the only grid: internal/backoff has no
# IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX branch and its three rows per kind are one retry decision,
# one interval and a whole retry chain.
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="Next Interval Chain"
DECIDED_ON="ns/op allocs/op"
# This family's decision cannot be taken from this family's measurement, and
# that is now declared rather than discovered. §9.1's evidence is a
# "retry-storm simulation (10k clients, 30 s outage): peak concurrency,
# time-to-recover", and it exists -- `BenchmarkBackoff/Storm/<kind>/
# clients=10000/outage=30s` in benchmarks/sim/retrystorm, which reports
# peak-concurrency and recover-s and is deterministic. But that is the nested
# `benchmarks` module and hack/bakeoff.sh runs `go test` in this family's PKG,
# which cannot reach it -- the same shape as family A29's benchmark
#  -- and its kind sits two segments below the root, where
# `splitKind` reads "Storm" as the kind for every row. So the campaign
# measures three microbenchmarks and ADR-018 must take the deciding numbers
# from a separate run:
#   (cd benchmarks && go test -run='^$' -bench='^BenchmarkBackoff/Storm' \
#      -benchtime=1x -count=1 ./sim/retrystorm)
# Assumption A24.69 records it and what it would take to fix.
CRITERION_GAP="peak-concurrency=benchmarks/sim/retrystorm BenchmarkBackoff/Storm, a nested module hack/bakeoff.sh cannot reach from this PKG (assumption A24.69); recover-s=benchmarks/sim/retrystorm BenchmarkBackoff/Storm (assumption A24.69)"
